  "reason": "Evidence strongly favors scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + multiprofile as the optimal backbone (config_021 at 0.7250 is the current best). The only remaining untested configuration with these two best encoders in multiprofile mode is config_034 (avgpool, concat). This experiment tests the other corner of the aggregation–fusion space: whether avgpool+concat can match or approach the transformer+weighted result (0.7250) or the transformer+concat result (0.7207, config_031). If config_034 lands near 0.72, it confirms that the specific aggregation/fusion choice is a secondary factor and the 0.7250 ceiling is robust; if it drops substantially, it confirms that transformer+weighted is the critical pairing. This is the best use of experiment 8 because it is the last meaningful untested variant within the proven-best encoder combination, reducing residual uncertainty about the design space before the final two experiments. Expected relative cost: moderate (~4–5 GPU hours), comparable to config_045 (4.82 h) since it uses the same imagenet_vit_l encoder with avgpool rather than the more expensive transformer aggregation."
